      }
    },
    {
      "body": "**Testing performed:**\n\nTested with GGUF models on RTX 5090 (32GB, Blackwell architecture):\n- bartowski/NousResearch_Hermes-4-14B-GGUF\n- tensorblock/Qwen_Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507-GGUF\n\nRan models through a local benchmark runner for HumanEval and GSM8K. Verified the semaphore leak fix by running repeated model load/unload cycles without resource exhaustion.\n\n**Related PRs:**\n\nThis is part of a series of GGUF pipeline fixes for Blackwell GPU compatibility:\n- #30410: Fix GGUF dtype selection for Blackwell compatibility\n- #30412 (this PR): Fix tokenizer semaphore leak\n- #30434: Shared memory barrier fix",
      "created_at": "2026-01-21T00:28:06Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/30412#issuecomment-3775569767",
      "id": 3775569767,
      "updated_at": "2026-01-21T00:28:06Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "kitaekatt"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "## Validation Results\n\n| vLLM | transformers | Cherry-picked PRs | HumanEval | IFEval |\n|------|-------------|-------------------|-----------|--------|\n| HEAD | 5.x | #30410, #30411, #30412, #30413, #30424, #30434, #30699, #30702, #31464, #33846 | gem2-2b-gguf (42.1%), gemma3-1b (26.8%) | gem2-2b-gguf (65.6%) |\n| HEAD | 4.x | #30410, #30411, #30412, #30413, #30424, #30434, #30699, #30702, #31464, #33846 | q3-moe-gguf (83.5%) | q3-moe-gguf (85.4%) |\n\nTested on RTX 5090 (Blackwell, SM 120) with all listed PRs cherry-picked together; models listed under each benchmark passed that benchmark in the given environment, while the same models crash or fail without these PRs applied.\n\nRebased to current upstream HEAD and re-validated on RTX 5090 (Blackwell, SM 120). Fix confirmed still necessary — gem2-2b-gguf and gemma3-1b (both with tied embeddings) crash without it.",
      "created_at": "2026-03-10T20:10:00Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/30412#issuecomment-4034143932",
      "id": 4034143932,
      "updated_at": "2026-03-10T20:10:00Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "kitaekatt"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Hi @22quinn @Isotr0py — this has been sitting without review for a while. Just rebased on latest `upstream/main` (merge commit), so the branch should now be mergeable. Quick summary:  Skip lm_head mapping for models with tied word embeddings:small fix in gguf_loader.py — tied-embedding models were failing when lm_head mapping was attempted. Rebased on latest main.\n\nWould appreciate a look when you have cycles. Thanks!",
      "created_at": "2026-04-18T21:28:22Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/30412#issuecomment-4274595276",
      "id": 4274595276,
      "updated_at": "2026-04-18T21:28:22Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "kitaekatt"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Went to check `_get_gguf_weights_map` against current `main` before reviewing the logic, and `vllm/model_executor/model_loader/gguf_loader.py` no longer exists there at all, the whole file is gone from `vllm/model_executor/model_loader/` (checked the directory listing directly, no gguf_loader.py, and no other file in that directory references GGUF weight mapping either). Whatever the fix here was meant to do, the target it's patching has since been removed or restructured, so this can't apply as-is regardless of whether the tied-embeddings logic itself is correct.\n\nMight be worth confirming whether GGUF loading was dropped/relocated and, if the underlying bug is still relevant, re-filing against wherever that logic lives now rather than rebasing this diff.\n",
